Package: oneplus-erhai-thermal
Version: 1.3
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Recommends: gnome-shell, polkitd
Description: Android-style whole-die CPU+GPU thermal governor for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 erhai-thermal.sh implements the same thermal architecture Android uses on this
 SoC: a userspace governor watches the whole-die envelope (CPU + GPU + NPU +
 DDR sensors) and, as it approaches the profile's switch-on trigger, writes
 cooling levels into the kernel cpufreq/devfreq cooling devices - the exact
 levels Android's thermal-engine-v2 produces under the Burnout benchmark
 (960/1018/734 MHz floors). The performance profile reproduces Android's
 measured 92-106C envelope under a full CPU+GPU+NPU load, which the old
 plane-local power_allocator tables could not (they were blind to NPU heat).
 Profiles selected via /etc/default/erhai-thermal; the boot service runs the
 governor; a template unit (erhai-thermal@.service) applies switches and a
 polkit ruleset lets the desktop user switch without a password. The
 erhai-thermal@erhai.local GNOME Shell extension exposes the switch in the
 Quick Settings. See /usr/share/oneplus-erhai-thermal/README.md.
